# Slice 284 probe: two dereference actuals, and a name followed by a dereference: `two(\px, \py)`, `two(y, \px)`.  Entry 7.
int: x 3
@: px int @ x
int: y 4
@: py int @ y
fn: two (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a * 10 + b
end: two
int: code 7
if: two(\px, \py) != 34
    code: 11
---
if: code = 7 && two(y, \px) != 43
    code: 12
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
